# AI 2027 — Thematic Analysis & Aggregated Roadmap

Oct 30, 2026 · @Kiss József

## Executive Summary

Across 8 transcripts, the consensus is that 2027 rewards judgment, communication and selling over technical execution, as agents make building close to free.

**Source key:** S1 Laurie Voss (Arize AI) · S2 "What I'd Learn Instead of AI Automation in 2027" (Nick, Maker School) · S3 "AI Consultant in 2027" (Nick, Maker School) · S4 "How To Survive The Next 2 Years" (unnamed ex-AI-company founder, 20 yrs in tech) · S5 "How to Survive the Next 2 Years" (unnamed; \[Inference\] likely the Maker School speaker) · S6 Matt Pocock interview (host: Nate Herk) · S7 James, software engineer of 14 years · S8 "The Last AI Roadmap Video" (Nick, Maker School).

- **The bottleneck has moved from writing code to defining "good".** Agents made code "basically free"; what stays human is finding out what people need and writing it down as specs, rubrics and evals (S1, S6, S3).
- **The engineering role is turning into "product engineer".** Forward-deployed engineer postings rose 800% in 9 months of 2025, averaging $240k (S1). Engineers who stay in delivery report becoming reviewers and QA for AI output (S7).
- **The junior ladder is broken now, not in the future.** Employment for 22–25-year-olds is falling (S1), 19% below trend in AI-exposed jobs (S5). Nobody in the document offers a scalable fix.
- **AI consulting peaks in 2027, then shifts.** S2 calls 2027 "probably the most profitable year" and possibly the start of decline. Work moves from building systems to workshops, team upskilling and strategic advice. The method is bottleneck-first (RACE plus goal factoring) (S2, S3).
- **Automation tooling is migrating.** Drag-and-drop builders (Zapier, Make, n8n, Power Automate) are declining in favour of agent harnesses, skills and scheduled routines. Automation benchmarks are nearing saturation (S2, S3, S8).
- **Distribution and sales beat technical skill.** S2 puts sales and marketing at "100x" the value of technical skill; S5 and S7 call distribution or a personal brand the portable hedge against layoffs.
- **Survival is layered.** Run a personal eval on every new model, prepare physical and digital security, build ownership and relationships, and anchor your identity in character rather than job title (S4, S5, S7).

